Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
a couple of days ago i was invited to a  digital viewing of eldon ring it  included new screenshots the opportunity  for q day but most importantly i got to  view this stunning 16-minute gameplay  showcase that i'm not allowed to show  you for some reason which is weird  because this showcase is really well  made so i can only assume that you'll  see it soon  until then though you have this video  which will mainly be audio only so  hey while you listen for free to tab out  and browse soul arts which is my new art  book project now on kickstarter the  first thing the player does is approach  this grace checkpoint so for those of  you who don't know these are elden rings  version of bonfires but there's more to  it than that  because the open world is so vast a  gentle ray of light will shine from the  grace pointing you towards your next  main objective to be clear this doesn't  mean that your next objective will be  easy so sometimes it might be wise to  ignore the guidance and strike out on  your own path you know looking for loot  if you feel like you need to become more  powerful first  at points of lost grace you can summon  the fire keeper maiden of this game who  i got to see in a cut scene she phases  in like a spirit just like your horse  does and she sits down and removes her  hood revealing this light strawberry  blonde hair  these olive eyes with one of them being  scarred and shut tight she introduces  herself as melina and offers you an  accord ending the cutscene  she's a nest here maiden you'll see in  my interview every journalist would have  learned different things from their  interview but in my interview it was  revealed that you can level up at  melinda and customize things like your  spirit summons and equipped weapon  skills while you sit at a grace graces  also refill this game's equivalent of an  estus flask but since graces are a  little bit harder to come by than  bonfires are you can also get a bit of  health back by defeating mobs of enemies  which from software says should keep you  exploring a little bit longer  beyond graces there is another more  traditional hub location and i'm showing  it on screen now here npcs you meet in  the outside world will come to visit you  similar to places like firelink shrine  in the center there's what looks like  this really large grace checkpoint and  it has threads connected to weapons that  are lying askew in the middle of the  table i was thinking that maybe every  time you find a grace in the outside  world a new thread is added or maybe the  light grows larger but that's just  speculation  around the table are chairs presumably  where npcs will come to sit  and i have to say this room is just so  visually distinct from other hub worlds  that we've seen before  it's ornate it's elegant and i think  that really befits a tarnished because  you are a character who is striving to  get this sort of dignity back  i love that after leaving the grace  checkpoint your character starts running  and they summon their mount while moving  with this smooth fast animation it's so  easy to imagine this being used mid  combat whenever you need a burst of  speed to get away or to close a gap and  once you see the player actually riding  around you get such a thrill from seeing  that because the previous trailer was  really good but it was cut so often that  you couldn't really get a sense of the  vastness of the world but in this video  you get to see the player transition  from exploring that open world into  exploring camps and dungeons and random  encounters around the place it just  feels so much more fulfilling to see the  game that way and unsurprisingly this  video revealed a ton of new information  during the presentation from software  made it clear that generally in terms of  horseback combat you might prefer to  fight on horseback when you're against  larger foes where hit and run tactics  are effective and you might prefer to  dismount to take out multiple enemies  more carefully  out of combat you and your horse have a  sprint that doesn't use up your stamina  and this is supposed to help you  traverse the world in combat however  stamina will come back into play and  then on horseback you can easily fire  arrows you can fire off sorcery and you  can of course swing your weapon so i was  shown horseback combat in a fight  against this giant wyvern which starts  as this small speck in the sky in the  distance and then flies down it  obliterates this group of hollows  standing nearby  and the fight begins  from software are calling these field  bosses they're mini bosses varying in  difficulty that can be fought in the  open world freely and the second field  boss in the trailer is fought at the end  of a co-op showcase and it fights  similarly to those dragon kin that are  in archdragon peak it it's capable of  extending its body in a really surreal  way and when the two characters defeat  this field boss it leaves behind a grace  checkpoint which i thought was  interesting at some point in the trailer  the player brings up the map which has  this really  beautiful honestly hand-drawn style  and looks absolutely gorgeous this map i  found from octopath traveler is the  closest thing i found  i obviously can't show the actual map  one of the most interesting things i  noticed on the map was this enormous  ocean area with ships and even what  looked like a path demarcated on it it  made me wonder if some sort of ocean  exploration is possible maybe swimming  is like it is in sakura and then also on  the map obviously you have your location  and the direction you're facing and from  software mentions that you can set  markers on the map to help you with  exploration they say you might prefer to  mark off a forest that has valuable  crafting ingredients so you can come  back later or maybe mark off places with  a dangerous boss you haven't defeated  yet marked areas on the map also show up  as pillars of light in the distance and  this helps you move closer towards them  this is similar to breath of the wild or  fortnite as well i think  you don't actually fill out this map by  exploring instead you collect map  fragments that are scattered around the  world they're clearly trying to build  out their loot tables here to encourage  exploration and to encourage uh dungeon  diving for example and finally once  you've discovered a location you can  easily just fast travel there all in all  the map is a big step up from the  previous map we got which was securos  a map that was pretty useless but i have  to say eldon ring is drawing heavily  from what they learned with securo that  much is so obvious you know they're  adding a jump button they're adding  stealth and both of these things play a  huge part in differentiating this game  from dark souls and you see that in the  combat section so this section has the  player dismount on a tall cliff they  pull out their binoculars and they start  to scout the enemy camp below them  planning their assault to complement  their stealth something called sleep  arrows have been added they allow you to  quietly incapacitate enemies from a  distance which gives you an opportunity  to sneak past them without having to  kill them although if you do want to  kill them you can just one shot them if  they're a lesser enemy while they're  asleep if that doesn't seem overpowered  enough you can attack midair like  insecure you can shoot your bow mid-air  as well  you're basically sakura wearing armor  both sakura and dark souls had combat  arts but in my opinion neither sakura or  dark souls got weapon arts right however  eldon ring might  in this game they're called skills and  they're like weapon arts except that  they can be assigned to any weapon in  this trailer the character performs wind  blasts from a scimitar and they deal a  thunderstrike from a pole arm i think  all of this stuff will help your  character feel really customized and  really themed as well  again you probably find these things  hidden around the world which adds to  the loot table in the game another set  of things you can find hidden around the  world are spirits of the deceased these  unlock different sets of npcs for  summoning and these can only be summoned  in difficult areas that have these  obelisks present some spirits are tanky  some are aggressive some arranged and  some appear to come as a swarm in one  example from the video the player  summoned a set of like six friendly npcs  these phantoms caused chaos they allowed  the player to weave in and out of all  the enemies they were facing and allow  the player to deal damage more freely  the player in this scene was dealing  damage with a twin blade by the way so  i'm glad they're bringing that back from  dark souls 2. according to from software  spirit summons use the fp system you'll  remember from dark souls basically the  mana system the strongest summons use  more fp and weaker summons use less this  might make it a bit less overpowered  than i thought at first  since if you summon spirits you might  not have access to your spells and  skills  still spirit summons are probably very  powerful by nature and i anticipate  elden ring in general will be far more  accessible to new players just because  you have so many ways of overcoming  adversity in this game a few sections of  the video showcase co-op and this is  something i'm really excited for because  it just seems less instanced than in  previous games in the video two players  sneak through the forest that you see in  this screenshot they're avoiding these  large terrifying creatures who are  patrolling the area and then later we  delve into this underground dungeon with  our partner and we're avoiding these  sends fortress star traps and ambushes  together  from software have previously mentioned  that they want to reduce the friction  required for co-op removing requirements  like having humanity or embers and i  just hope they take this all the way i  hope they make it easy to bring our  friends into our world and then keep  them there i did notice that after  defeating a field boss your partner  didn't seem to disappear finally we make  our way to stormvale castle the legacy  dungeon of this first open world if the  open world of eldon ring is like dark  souls with a horse then legacy dungeons  are dark souls with a jump because from  what i saw they're way more vertically  inclined than ever before with multiple  paths sprawling left and right and these  paths are laid up and down as well  a character talks to an npc as soon as  they arrive at the castle and the npc  recommends that we take the back way  into the castle the player however opts  for the main gate instead and they're  instantaneously shot down by ballista  arrow fire i think you could roll  through this but our player quickly  changes their mind and they take the  back way instead the back way through  the castle has way more sakura elements  you're using jumps to get over rubble  you're avoiding guards that signal the  alarm and you're using sleep arrows to  sneak past giant enemies and waiting for  you at the end of all of this is the  heavily armed demigod whose full intro  cinematic we get to see this time one of  the really cool things i noticed here  was a new sort of counter-attack  animation that can be performed after  blocking it's this one from the earlier  trailer  basically when you block an attack in  alden ring with a weapon it seems like  you can quickly follow up with a unique  attack animation and i love this idea  because in dark souls whenever you  blocked an attack with your weapon it  didn't go well you know it did a lot of  stamina damage it did a lot of chip  damage but now in elden ring there is an  offensive benefit to blocking an attack  like this with a weapon it's not ideal  but it helps you get back into combat  and keep that pace going so in  conclusion i kind of take back what i  said about this not being big dark souls  elden ring is kind of big dark souls but  it's also secular souls way more than i  expected actually and it really does  feel like the culmination of everything  that they've learned up to this point  and  i think everyone who has seen this  footage will echo that sentiment i just  can't wait for you to see it i think  it's a bit silly that it hasn't been  shown publicly but anyway before i go i  want to ask would you guys listen to an  audiobook if i narrated it i'm asking  this because soon you will have the  opportunity to  a couple of weeks ago i revealed our  kickstarter for soul arts which is this  premium art book filled with all of the  best art from the art competitions i've  been running the last few years it's  also a book filled with short stories on  every page and now as a reward for all  the support you guys have given that  project i'm planning on narrating the  entire thing for backers to enjoy on  youtube this is a new part of the  digital edition of the book which almost  every single backer will have access to  by default  so please enjoy the hinterlands it's one  of many short stories that i'm writing  for soul arts enjoy  the player begins a journey through the  outskirts of the hinterlands a murky  wetland brimming with decay and rot  once the hinterlands were home to the  crows a wise and perceptive clan  renowned for wielding weapons forged  from cyderite they coveted this shining  metal and would go to great lengths to  obtain it stashing it in their homes for  safe keeping it was said to have fallen  from the sky and the crows worshiped  anything that originated from such a  heavenly realm  one day a herald arrived in their  primitive town preaching of blood  healing and exceptional medicine  developed in a nearby town called yarnam  the crows had no need of such a thing  and the herald soon left  not long after his visit the land  softened crops started to wilt and crows  fell afflicted by a strange illness that  had them coughing blood and ash  suspecting a ploy to empty their town so  it could be pillaged of ciderite the  remaining tribes folk departed for yanum  nevertheless forced from the place they  once called home their sick required  healing but a crow never forgets the  face and the healing church will rue  their murder  you

